  "title": "Chapter 38: Natural Vegetation of India",
  "order": 38,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sp72h7l",
      "content": "Natural vegetation refers to plant life that grows naturally in a region without human interference. It depends mainly on climate, rainfall, soil, altitude and relief. India's diverse geography supports a wide variety of vegetation types and wildlife."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
