    {
      "id": "exzcw2z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Natural vegetation distribution across India is determined by various physical and climatic factors.",
        "Major vegetation types include Tropical Evergreen, Tropical Deciduous, Thorn, Mountain, and Mangrove forests.",
        "Deciduous and Thorn forests adapt specifically to variations in rainfall patterns.",
        "Mangrove forests are vital coastal vegetation ecosystems located in delta regions."
      ],
      "id": "57jjrds"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nck09is",
      "content": "• Climate – Temperature and rainfall determine vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g9br4z4",
      "content": "• Soil – Different soils support different plants."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "poq1rsu",
      "content": "• Relief – Plains, plateaus and mountains influence vegetation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hqapkan",
      "content": "• Altitude – Vegetation changes with height in mountain regions."
    },
    {
